how can buying property in coventry  basingstoke and milton keynes possibly  help people living in mid-suffolk and  baby  back in 2017  baber and mid-suffolk district councils  created sifco limited a commercial  property investment company designed  purely to generate money to be  reinvested in council services  the councils borrowed 50 million pounds  each and lent it to cifco so cifco could  buy a portfolio of properties  sifco now manages this portfolio  collecting rent from its tenants  it then pays the councils more than  enough to pay back their loan repayments  plus money on top for the councils to  reinvest in services and projects such  as helping the recovery of the local  economy supporting communities and  combating climate change so how's it  performing so far sifko has brought in  more than five million pounds in extra  income for baber and mid-suffolk and  more than two million of that was during  2020 2021 despite the impact of covet  that's all money that we can use to  support our districts  but hasn't sifko made massive losses  there were always costs involved in  buying property and when you invest 100  million pounds you can expect fees and  stamp duty to also add up to millions  we've also seen the value of some  properties fall  meaning cifco has recorded a 4.5 million  pound loss for 2020 2021  but this is what's known as a paper loss  because it would only happen if we sold  the whole portfolio tomorrow and we  won't be doing that the portfolio is a  long-term legacy for residents  generating income for years to come with  sifko gradually repaying the loan so  these properties will ultimately be  owned debt free by baber and mid-suffolk  district councils  but isn't this risky  cifco was careful about which properties  it brought  making sure there was a mix of  industrial commercial and retail across  the uk to reduce the impact of any  disaster across any particular sector or  area  sifko's performance goes through  rigorous regular scrutiny by elected  councillors and the company needs the  agreement of both councils each year to  carry out its plans for the next 12  months  these debates and votes are live  streamed for everyone to see  sifko's accounts are independently  audited and the details of the full  portfolio and quarterly statistics are  all publicly available on cifco's  website  so  you can be sure that the councils are  keeping a close eye on their investments  and that the professionals at sifko as  well as the external experts who advise  them are making sure these properties  continue to bring in money for baber and  mid-suffix communities for many years to  come
 

